  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 136 PM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nMonday night into Tuesday...The disturbance over the Four Corners \nwill move into and through the region. This will bring an increase \nin mid and high cloudiness. Remains a dry forecast, with\nshowers,if any, expected to remain southeast of the area. Surface\nlow pressure deepening along the Front Range will bring a \nreturn of southerly winds 10 to 20 mph in the afternoon. Highs \nwarmer from the upper 60s to lower 70s.\n\nWednesday and beyond...Upper troughing will persist across the \nwestern U.S. with a closed low of the coast of southern California \nby Wednesday. Upper ridging will amplify into Thursday across the \nCentral U.S. Highs warm into the 70s Wednesday and Thursday. \nThursday night through Saturday, the western US upper trough/closed \nlow will advance east across the Rockies by late Friday, bringing an \nincrease in moisture, with dewpoints in the 50s Thursday night and \nFriday. Could see a few showers in advance of the system Thursday \nnight, with increased chances for showers and a few thunderstorms \nFriday afternoon through Saturday. A cold front is forecast to move \ninto the area Saturday. Highs in the 70s to near 80 Friday, cool \ninto the 60s to near 70 by next Saturday.",
